.TH CLIPGUM 1 "October 2026" "ClipGum 1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
clipgum \- deterministic, local-only text transformations
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B clipgum
.I command
.RI [ options ]
.RI [ file ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B clipgum
reads UTF-8 text from a named file or standard input and writes the requested transformation to standard output. It does not read the system pasteboard, start a daemon, open a network connection, or invoke a shell. A file input uses mapped data when safe; standard input is consumed in bounded chunks.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B clean-secrets
Redact API keys, bearer tokens, provider tokens, internal hostnames, and valid IPv4 addresses.
.TP
.B sanitize-text
Strip known URL tracking parameters and redact secrets.
.TP
.B strip-urls
Remove known tracking query parameters while preserving unrelated URL bytes.
.TP
.B json-to-ts
Infer a deterministic TypeScript type from JSON. Use
.B --root-name
to select the root identifier.
.TP
.B extract-table
Parse CSV, TSV, or semicolon-delimited text with quoted-field support and emit normalized CSV.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B --raw
Do not append a trailing newline to raw text output.
.TP
.B --diff
Emit a unified text diff instead of transformed text.
.TP
.B --json
Emit a JSON object containing the operation, output, and change count. Cannot be combined with
.BR --diff .
.TP
.B --locale \fIidentifier\fR
Set a locale override for locale-aware operations. Current transformations are locale invariant and do not make network locale requests.
.TP
.B --root-name \fIname\fR
Set the TypeScript root identifier for
.BR json-to-ts .
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
cat log.txt | clipgum clean-secrets | pbcopy
clipgum json-to-ts < schema.json
clipgum sanitize-text --json < note.txt
clipgum clean-secrets --diff dump.txt
.fi
.SH POLICY
When the managed ForceSecretRedaction preference is true, strict redaction is applied again after the requested transformation and before standard output is written. This protects pipelines that end in pbcopy.
.SH LIMITS
Input is limited to 64 MiB and must be UTF-8. JSON and table transforms have a 16 MiB deterministic parser boundary. Startup latency and memory use vary by machine; no universal sub-15 ms claim is made without measurement.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR pbcopy (1),
.BR pbpaste (1)
